  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Information:\nCurrently facing a bug in which any video, livestreamed or normal, will start loud compared to what it should be.\n\nSteps to replicate:\nCreate your standard VRC_Sync Video Stream and audio source.\nDisable the game object present on the audio source, but not the audio source component itself.\nEnable the object via a trigger.\n\nExpected outcome:\nAudio will be loud and audible from any location, disabling and re-enabling the gameobject via the trigger will fix this, it will only occur once per current instance session (user must rejoin for such to occur again).\n\nAdditional information:\nI am using a local enable trigger.\nIt is a standard audio source with nothing attached to it, i've attempted to use ONSP and the audio mixer, neither changed anything.\nIt seems to only occur on streamed audio, as the audio is constantly syncing with the video sync, it plays the audio with no delays inbetween which verifies this, whereas a standard direct file, will instead reset everytime the game object is disabled, and as such seems to not be affected by it.",
